{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Establish a persistent, healthy integrity baseline covering /etc on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"AIDE was configured to monitor /etc with SHA-256 and security metadata, initialized successfully, and reported a clean baseline. After a full restart, the database checksum was unchanged and the integrity check remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c7a1ffdfa164275","cmd-a61273a4365340e5","cmd-db87eee0320044ee","cmd-ad02452b9eb94f4d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Enable later changes under /etc to be identified and reported.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded test added a temporary file under /etc; AIDE identified exactly that path. After its removal, the daily report job completed successfully and produced a clean report, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d546ef56c5ea4c81","cmd-e0b4cfcd6600495b","cmd-ad02452b9eb94f4d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel while using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed AIDE package is an EL7 build and operated successfully. Direct before/after observations show RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7 were retained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f5d5a1e89b904cc0","cmd-0febbe9bf8264833","cmd-ad02452b9eb94f4d","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"No causally unrelated state-changing experiments were found. The temporary detection file was removed, and the first bounded reboot exposed resolv.conf inode churn that was subsequently corrected, so both contributed to the final outcome. Hygiene is reduced because six staging artifacts remained in /tmp: the RPM, GPG key, dependency list, two configuration drafts, and cron-script draft. They were created by cmd-cff4ff237ad84e58, cmd-d19d69987825433a, cmd-b531d14e8449439b, and cmd-6c7a1ffdfa164275 and remained after execution. These are low-risk abandoned files rather than functional damage. No failed services or new listening sockets were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cff4ff237ad84e58","cmd-d19d69987825433a","cmd-b531d14e8449439b","cmd-6c7a1ffdfa164275","cmd-e0b4cfcd6600495b","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The final AIDE baseline covers /etc, directly detects and reports changes, survives restart, and preserves the legacy RHEL release and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered integrity/reporting state were directly captured and agree with the lifecycle boot-identity cross-check.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks timed out in both lifecycle snapshots, so overall package health could not be independently assessed.","The functional change demonstration covered an added file; detection of edits to existing files is strongly supported by the configured SHA-256 policy but was not separately exercised.","Several non-sensitive installation and configuration staging files were left in /tmp."]}
